  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 346 AM EST Tue Nov 24 2026\n\nThe frontal boundary and shortwave axis will move east of the area \non Thursday. Residual moisture will keep the chance of showers in \nthe forecast through at least the first half of the day. High \npressure and much drier air will filter into the region for Friday \nand Saturday. Attention then turns to a cut off low over the eastern \nPacific on Thursday which will cut across Mexico on Friday and \nSaturday and enter the Gulf late Saturday into early Sunday. This \nfeature will eventually get absorbed into the larger upper level \ntrough moving eastward across the country. There are some timing \ndifferences between the global models, but rain chances should \nreturn to South FL on Sunday or Monday next week. \n\nBelow normal temps are expected Friday and Saturday before \nrebounding back to near normal Sunday and early next week as the \nnext system arrives.",
